Package: shoal
Title: High-Performance Clustering via Rust
Version: 0.0.0.1
Authors@R:
    person("First", "Last", , "first.last@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A small, foundational set of clustering algorithms with Rust
    backends, presented behind one consistent interface: k-means and Gaussian
    mixtures via 'linfa', the density-based methods DBSCAN and HDBSCAN via
    'petal-clustering', agglomerative hierarchical clustering via 'kodama',
    EVoC, direct multi-granularity clustering of embedding vectors, via an
    in-tree port of the reference implementation, and graph SLIC superpixels
    over any point set with a neighbour graph. All algorithms return
    objects sharing a common class, so printing and plotting behave
    identically whichever algorithm produced the result.
